"""Build the offline exact-state and upper-bound page; standard library only."""
from pathlib import Path
from html import escape
import json
HERE=Path(__file__).resolve().parent

def math(tex,display=False):return '<span class="math'+(' display' if display else '')+'" data-tex="'+escape(tex,quote=True)+'">'+escape(tex)+'</span>'
def links(folder,items):return '<div class="links">'+''.join('<a href="'+folder+'/'+file+'">'+label+' ↓</a>' for file,label in items)+'</div>'
def main():
 states=json.loads((HERE/'states.json').read_text())['states'];by={r['n']:r for r in states}
 basic=[('proof.tex','Complete LaTeX proof'),('certificate.json','Certificate'),('independent-verification.json','Independent verification report'),('certificate-bundle.zip','Complete portable bundle')]
 out='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>27–30 qubits · Exact AC states and upper bounds</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../styles.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.css"><script src="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.js" defer></script><style>main{max-width:1060px;padding-block:40px}h1{font-size:clamp(32px,5vw,48px)}h2{margin-top:40px}.display{display:block;overflow-x:auto;padding:12px 0}.links{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px 20px;margin-block:20px}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%}th,td{text-align:left;padding:12px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.claim{padding:18px 22px;background:var(--paper-alt,#f0efe9);border-left:3px solid var(--accent,#5e4b7c)}pre{overflow-x:auto;padding:14px;background:var(--paper-alt,#f0efe9)}section{scroll-margin-top:24px}</style></head><body><main><a href="../../index.html">← Pure AC-state catalogue</a><p class="eyebrow">Exact states · Universal exclusions</p><h1>Twenty-seven to thirty qubits</h1><p class="claim">The maximum pure AC order is six at N=28 and seven at N=30. New exact fifth-order states are also available at N=27 and N=29; their maximum-order questions remain unresolved within the bounds below.</p>'''
 out+='<table><thead><tr><th>Qubits</th><th>Exact attained order</th><th>Maximum pure order</th><th>Construction</th></tr></thead><tbody>'
 for n,t,upper in [(27,5,6),(28,6,6),(29,5,6),(30,7,7)]:
  bound=f't_{{\\max}}({n})={t}' if t==upper else f'{t}\\le t_{{\\max}}({n})\\le {upper}'
  out+='<tr><th><a href="#n'+str(n)+'">'+str(n)+'</a></th><td>'+str(t)+'</td><td>'+math(bound)+'</td><td>'+('Certified isolated algebraic root' if n==28 else 'Explicit radical Dicke coefficients')+'</td></tr>'
 out+='</tbody></table><p>Existence and universal upper bounds are proved separately. Failed numerical searches are not exclusion proofs. Original numerical library records retain their numerical coefficient evidence.</p>'
 out+='<details><summary>Numerical work on the remaining sixth-order cases</summary><p>Full complex-state searches and four- and five-copy positivity tests did not produce an order-six state or a rigorous exclusion at N=27 or N=29. The rigorous interval remains 5–6 for both. Small numerical residuals are not used as proofs.</p><p><a href="order6-search-report.json">Read the scoped numerical research report ↓</a></p></details>'
 for n in (27,29):
  rec=by[n];out+='<section id="n'+str(n)+'"><h2>'+str(n)+' qubits: an explicit fifth-order state</h2><p>With normalized Dicke vectors, set</p>'+math(rec['parametersLatex'],True)+math(rec['stateLatex'].removeprefix(r'\begin{gathered}').split(r'\\[6pt]')[0],True)
  defect=rec['verification']['nextOrderWitness']['differenceLatex'];out+='<p>Independent exact direct partial traces give</p>'+math(r'\rho_5=I_6/6,\qquad(\rho_6)_{00}-1/7='+defect+r'\ne0.',True)
  if n==29:out+='<p>The order is exactly five. This representative has two double Majorana poles and 25 simple finite points, giving the partition '+math(r'(2^2,1^{25})')+'. It differs from the all-simple numerical library representative.</p>'
  else:out+='<p>The order is exactly five, and all 27 Majorana points are distinct. A reciprocal-polynomial argument proves the multiplicities exactly.</p>'
  t=7
  out+='<h3>What the upper bound settles</h3><p>A rigorously validated four-copy positivity certificate, supplemented by partial-transpose constraints for N=29, excludes every pure order-'+str(t)+' AC state. Exact factorial contractions and outward-rounded interval bounds cover arbitrary complex amplitudes. The maximum is therefore '+math(r'5\le t_{\max}('+str(n)+r')\le'+str(t-1))+'. Sixth-order existence remains unresolved by this catalogue.</p>'
  out+='<p><a href="../../index.html#n='+str(n)+'&amp;t=5&amp;state='+rec['id']+'">Open the exact state and Majorana viewer ↗</a></p>'+links('n'+str(n)+'-t'+str(t),basic+[('verify_certificate.py','Validated independent verifier')])+'</section>'
 out+='<section id="n28"><h2>28 qubits: maximum order six</h2><p>A rational contraction certificate defines a unique exact algebraic state near the refined Liège representative:</p>'+math(by[28]['stateLatex'],True)
 out+='<p>The certificate fixes nine rational coordinates and isolates the remaining 49 coordinates by 49 rational quadratic equations equivalent to '+math(r'\rho_6=I_7/7')+'. Its radius is '+math(r'10^{-65}')+'. An independent standard-library verifier reconstructs the equations, exact Jacobian and approximate-inverse defect, then proves strict self-mapping and contraction. The root has algebraic coordinates; closed-form radical components are not claimed.</p>'+math(r'\|AF(x^0)\|_\infty<10^{-66},\quad\|I-ADF(x^0)\|_\infty<10^{-76},\quad q<10^{-53}.',True)
 out+='<p>A rational interval also proves '+math(r'(\rho_7)_{00}-1/8<-1/40000')+' for this root. The displayed decimal components and nearby Majorana coordinates are numerical renderings of the exact definition.</p><h3>The universal upper bound</h3><p>A separate rigorously validated four-copy positivity certificate excludes every seventh-order pure symmetric state. This proves '+math(r't_{\max}(28)=6')+' together with the exact sixth-order state.</p><p><a href="../../index.html#n=28&amp;t=6&amp;state=certified-algebraic-n28-t6">Open the certified state and Majorana viewer ↗</a></p>'
 out+=links('n28-t6',[('proof.tex','Exact algebraic existence proof'),('certificate.json','Rational root certificate'),('verify_independently.py','Standard-library existence verifier'),('independent-verification.json','Exact existence report')])+links('n28-t7',basic+[('verify_certificate.py','Validated independent exclusion verifier')])
 out+='<details><summary>Additional eighth-order exclusion</summary><p>This exact three-copy upper bound is retained as an auxiliary result. The stronger seventh-order exclusion above settles the maximum.</p>'+links('n28-t8',basic+[('verify_independently.py','Exact independent verifier')])+'</details></section>'
 out+='<section id="n30"><h2>30 qubits: maximum order seven</h2><p>Two octahedral binary forms give a compact radical construction:</p>'+math(r'F_6=z(1-z^4),\qquad F_8=1+14z^4+z^8,',True)+math(by[30]['parametersLatex'],True)+math(r'c_r=\frac{[z^r]\bigl(\alpha F_6^5+\beta F_6F_8^3\bigr)}{\sqrt{\binom{30}r}},\qquad |\psi_{30}\rangle=\sum_{r=0}^{30}c_r|D_{30}^{(r)}\rangle.',True)
 out+='<p>Only eight Dicke components are nonzero. Exact Schmidt reductions and an independent direct partial trace prove</p>'+math(r'\rho_7=I_8/8,\qquad(\rho_8)_{00}-1/9=-\frac{11}{538200}\ne0.',True)
 out+='<p>All 30 Majorana points are distinct, proved by a polynomial gcd after extracting the six octahedral vertices.</p><h3>The universal upper bound</h3><p>An exact rational three-copy positivity certificate excludes every eighth-order pure symmetric state. The independent verifier reconstructs all physical contraction equations, the separating identity, and positive matrices. Hence '+math(r't_{\max}(30)=7')+'.</p><p><a href="../../index.html#n=30&amp;t=7&amp;state=octahedral-n30-t7">Open the exact state and Majorana viewer ↗</a></p>'+links('n30-t8',basic+[('verify_independently.py','Exact independent exclusion verifier')])+'</section>'
 out+='<section id="reproduce"><h2>Reproduce the constructions and proofs</h2><p>The radical-state verifier requires SymPy. The N28 existence and both three-copy exclusion verifiers require only Python’s standard library. The validated four-copy exclusion verifiers require NumPy and python-flint (Arb); they independently reconstruct the representation and use outward-rounded interval arithmetic.</p><pre><code>python3 radical-witnesses/verify_witnesses.py\npython3 n28-t6/verify_independently.py\npython3 n27-t7/verify_certificate.py\npython3 n28-t7/verify_certificate.py\npython3 n29-t7/verify_certificate.py\npython3 n30-t8/verify_independently.py</code></pre>'
 out+=links('radical-witnesses',[('proof.tex','Analytical radical constructions'),('states.json','Exact radical Dicke components'),('build_witnesses.py','Portable radical builder'),('verify_witnesses.py','Independent direct-trace verifier'),('independent-verification.json','Exact verification report')])+links('.', [('states.json','Combined state records'),('proofs.json','Upper-bound proof records'),('build_states.py','Rebuild state records and renderings'),('build_page.py','Rebuild this page'),('MANIFEST.txt','File checksums')])+'</section>'
 out+='</main><script>document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded",()=>{for(const el of document.querySelectorAll("[data-tex]"))katex.render(el.dataset.tex,el,{displayMode:el.classList.contains("display"),throwOnError:true});});</script></body></html>'
 (HERE/'index.html').write_text(out)
 print('Built offline research page: maxima N28=6,N30=7; gaps N27=5–6,N29=5–6.')
if __name__=='__main__':main()
